o the plane\n\n$$\nr=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 17 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+s[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,t,\\,s\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429817 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3c3b23dc-4bcb-57b2-b0fc-dd67734d3e36" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429817 #edb/ref 1074 "From the parametric equation, we have that $v=⟨2,-7,1⟩$ and $w=⟨3,5,0⟩$ are parallel to the plane.\n\nNow, we need to find a normal vector of the plane. To do that, we use the cross product of $v$ and $w$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\times [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -7 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-5i+3j+31k \\\\  & =⟨-5,3,31⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨-5,3,31⟩.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429818 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186429815 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429818 #edb/ref 1069 "q-158107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429818 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429818 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the volume of the $4$-dimensional parallelepiped spanned by the vectors\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,c=[\\begin{aligned}13 \\\\ 11 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],\\,d=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429818 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8d62e579-1b65-5746-996a-3e6e877f180c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429818 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's construct the matrix $M,$ whose columns are the coordinates of our vectors $a,$ $b,$ $c,$ and  $d:$\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 13 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe volume of the parallelepiped spanned by these vectors equals the absolute value of the determinant of $M:$\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|\n$$\n\nThe determinant of a triangular matrix is equal to the product of the entries on the main diagonal. So, we have\n\n$$\ndet(M)=[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 & 13 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 11 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=(-7)\\cdot (-2)\\cdot (-5)\\cdot 1=-70.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the volume is\n\n$$\nV=|det(M)|=|-70|=70.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429943 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429944 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429945 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186429946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1045 "The Parametric Equations of a Plane" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186429946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050308 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429934 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "f1f3e620-4475-5a3a-a265-6ab29906aca2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429935 #edb/ref 1080 "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,-2,5⟩+t⟨-3,4,5⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429935 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429935 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "076c0841-49e0-5efa-932b-cea12451f354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429936 #edb/ref 1080 "r=⟨1,0,-2⟩+s⟨-2,-2,5⟩+t⟨-2,4,3⟩,\\,s,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429936 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429936 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "36f17219-1319-57b9-b736-3daca3fe9f64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186429937 #edb/ref 1080 "r